{:edb/db-before-t 2536 :edb/db-after-t 2537 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535849 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:56:05.393Z" 13194139535849 true] [17592186124358 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370019 13194139535849 true] [17592186124568 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370009 13194139535849 true] [17592186124574 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370012 13194139535849 true] [17592186124575 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370031 13194139535849 true] [17592186157355 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370026 13194139535849 true] [17592186192615 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370003 13194139535849 true] [17592186198338 1020 #edb/ref 17592186370006 13194139535849 true] [17592186370003 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370004 13194139535849 true] [17592186370003 1089 "q-168862" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370003 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535849 true] [17592186370003 1100 "A company produces two types of products, type A and type B. The revenue function of the company, in thousands of dollars, is given by $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2,\n$$\n\nwhere $x={[\\begin{aligned}\\,x & y\\,\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ $x$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product A, and $y$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product B. The company can adjust the prices per unit for both types of products by adding or removing certain features.\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370003 1113 #uuid "3d3ccd66-44cc-5858-a138-7ed8bb28ce89" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370003 1145 "We differentiate the given function with respect to $y,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the sum rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{x}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the constant multiple rule for differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(5{x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(10{y}^{2}) & =-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{4})-5{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})+10\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}) \\\\  & =-4{y}^{3}-5{x}^{2}\\cdot 2y+10\\cdot 2y \\\\  & =-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370004 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370005 13194139535849 true] [17592186370004 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535849 true] [17592186370004 1041 "field-1" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370004 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370005 13194139535849 true] [17592186370004 1110 #uuid "502c717a-d842-5e34-9bdc-c92c507605a3" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370005 1034 "-4y^3-10x^2y+20y" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535849 true] [17592186370005 1111 #uuid "e1cda81b-0f3b-5ddc-9e2d-0f726b2f7108" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370006 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370007 13194139535849 true] [17592186370006 1089 "q-168863" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370006 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535849 true] [17592186370006 1100 "A company produces two types of products, type A and type B. The revenue function of the company, in thousands of dollars, is given by $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2,\n$$\n\nwhere $x={[\\begin{aligned}\\,x & y\\,\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ $x$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product A, and $y$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product B. The company can adjust the prices per unit for both types of products by adding or removing certain features.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4y^3-10x^2y+20y$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $[$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y]$" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370006 1113 #uuid "348adeb4-b04c-5633-ac26-62027737b33e" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370006 1145 "For our scalar function, we have that\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)={(∇f)}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEarlier, we found that \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y.\n$$\n\nThe partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2)=-10x{y}^{2}-4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,-10x{y}^{2}-4x\\, & \\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370007 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370008 13194139535849 true] [17592186370007 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535849 true] [17592186370007 1041 "field-1" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370007 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370008 13194139535849 true] [17592186370007 1110 #uuid "ca79d037-a0b6-5722-9434-642337786b8d" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370008 1034 "-10xy^2-4x" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535849 true] [17592186370008 1111 #uuid "6e7e9fe4-ba19-5f71-9ae0-b2f1d54f558e" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370009 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370010 13194139535849 true] [17592186370009 1089 "q-168864" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370009 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535849 true] [17592186370009 1100 "A company produces two types of products, type A and type B. The revenue function of the company, in thousands of dollars, is given by $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2,\n$$\n\nwhere $x={[\\begin{aligned}\\,x & y\\,\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ $x$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product A, and $y$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product B. The company can adjust the prices per unit for both types of products by adding or removing certain features.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4y^3-10x^2y+20y$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $[$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-10xy^2-4x$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y]$\n\nCurrent part:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071276/assets/23b3e3c6e8eeecb32b38e868114bd2967882c5542edcfbee7f31f6e4a26d22da.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Given a sketch of the graph of $z=f(x)$ above, which of the points ($A,$ $B,$ or $C$) is a local maximum of the function?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        A local maximum is the point \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." 13194139535849 true] [17592186370009 1113 #uuid "0faa166d-d182-5da3-97cc-a09b62ab6189" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370009 1145 "A function $f(x,y)$ has a local maximum point at $(a,b)$ if $f(x,y)\\le f(a,b)$ for all points $(x,y)$ in a neighborhood of $(a,b).$ \n\nIn other words, we can take a neighborhood of $(x,y)$-values such that the point $(x,y,f(x,y))$ is the highest point on the graph in the neighborhood.\n\nAmong the given options, such neighborhoods exist for the point $A.$ Hence, $A$ is a local maximum .\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071276/assets/d19c97886c1449b414939269d9f9bf5d7ca8b418268ed5ef9b5940acaf29dbf7.png)" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370011 13194139535849 true] [17592186370010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535849 true] [17592186370010 1041 "field-1" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370010 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370011 13194139535849 true] [17592186370010 1110 #uuid "cb4b5327-8c1e-5e63-9fdc-c35bc2e1e6af" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370011 1034 "A" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535849 true] [17592186370011 1111 #uuid "30e35172-4ca0-590e-aa3c-728674f05a16" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370013 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370015 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1017 #edb/ref 17592186370017 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1089 "q-168865" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1100 "A company produces two types of products, type A and type B. The revenue function of the company, in thousands of dollars, is given by $f:{R}^{2}\\to R,$ defined as\n\n$$\nf(x)=-{y}^{4}-5{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+10{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}+2,\n$$\n\nwhere $x={[\\begin{aligned}\\,x & y\\,\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ $x$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product A, and $y$ is the price (in thousands of dollars) per unit of product B. The company can adjust the prices per unit for both types of products by adding or removing certain features.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\,=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-4y^3-10x^2y+20y$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $[$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-10xy^2-4x$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y]$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14071276/assets/23b3e3c6e8eeecb32b38e868114bd2967882c5542edcfbee7f31f6e4a26d22da.png)     \n                                \n                            \n\n   \n\n                            Given a sketch of the graph of $z=f(x)$ above, which of the points ($A,$ $B,$ or $C$) is a local maximum of the function?\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        A local maximum is the point \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        A                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe critical points of $f$ are$\\,$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $($ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,\\pm $ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$ and $($ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n, 0$).$" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1113 #uuid "2878166c-6222-50f8-90d4-be5415e8122e" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370012 1145 "The critical points of a multivariable function $f$ are the points $a$ in the domain of $f$ such that ${f}^{′}(a)={0}^{T}$ or ${f}^{′}(a)$ does not exist, where\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(a)={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂f}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}]|}_{x=a}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, the domain of $f$ is ${R}^{2},$ and the first derivative of $f$ is\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}-10x{y}^{2}-4x & \\,-4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the critical points, we need to find the points $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ such that ${f}^{′}(x,y)={0}^{T}$ or ${f}^{′}(x,y)$ does not exist. Note that, in our case, ${f}^{′}(x,y)$ exists everywhere, so we just need to find the points where ${f}^{′}(x,y)={0}^{T}.$\n\nSetting ${f}^{′}(x,y)={0}^{T},$ we have the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-10x{y}^{2}-4x=0 \\\\ -4{y}^{3}-10{x}^{2}y+20y=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-2x(5{y}^{2}+2)=0 \\\\ -2y(2{y}^{2}+5{x}^{2}-10)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $5{y}^{2}+2\\ne 0,$ from the first equation of the system, we obtain that\n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y(2{y}^{2}+5{x}^{2}-10) & =0 \\\\ -2y(2{y}^{2}+5(0)^{2}-10) & =0 \\\\ -4y({y}^{2}-5) & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\pm \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the critical points $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$ and $(0,0).$\n\nNote that since ${f}^{′}(x)={0}^{T}$ at these points, they are also stationary points." 13194139535849 true] [17592186370013 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370014 13194139535849 true] [17592186370013 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535849 true] [17592186370013 1041 "field-1" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370013 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370014 13194139535849 true] [17592186370013 1110 #uuid "e64e1506-7dbc-5180-bd74-d6a8994ced09" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370014 1034 "0" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535849 true] [17592186370014 1111 #uuid "c237b7dc-f9ac-5d0f-b84c-c02be9487e23" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370015 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370016 13194139535849 true] [17592186370015 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535849 true] [17592186370015 1041 "field-2" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370015 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370016 13194139535849 true] [17592186370015 1110 #uuid "7888bf8a-e521-5766-9e92-fd47b8faf624" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370016 1034 "\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370016 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535849 true] [17592186370016 1111 #uuid "7298a49f-ccc4-5f5f-9f6f-3f7e142699d1" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186370018 13194139535849 true] [17592186370017 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535849 true] [17592186370017 1041 "field-3" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186370018 13194139535849 true] [17592186370017 1110 #uuid "5975c673-fc2a-5350-8c8b-96085fb10705" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370018 1034 "0" 13194139535849 true] [17592186370018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535849 true] [17592186370018 1111 #uuid "16fdedf1-f44d-5062-a